What is Glacial Acrylic Acid?
Glacial Acrylic Acid (GAA) is a high-purity form of acrylic acid with a concentration typically exceeding 99%. It is a clear, colorless liquid with an acrid odor, miscible with water, alcohols, and ethers. Chemically represented as CH₂=CHCO₂H, it functions as both an unsaturated monocarboxylic acid and a vinyl compound, enabling diverse reactions for polymer production and chemical synthesis. Primarily used in the production of superabsorbent polymers, polyacrylates, and other derivatives, it plays a crucial role in industries such as personal care, construction, and water treatment.

